⍝ EXAMPLES.md section 3, level 1: the same program quoted and run under
⍝ the base interpreter.  `flipA` and `pair` are level-0 names, so inside
⍝ ⟨ ⟩ they are inlined as their expanded terms and then quoted; S, K and
⍝ I inside ⟨ ⟩ are the object type's leaves.
term ≡ S ∣ K ∣ I ∣ App term term
maybe ≡ Nothing ∣ Just term

whnfF ≔ { step m = sp m nil stepS stepK stepI }

swap p ≔* [3⊑p 2⊑p]
flipA q = swap q

prog   ≔ ⟨flipA [K I] K⟩
answer ≔ whnfF ⊢ ⟨flipA [K I] K⟩₄₁
short  ≔ whnfF ⊢ ⟨flipA [K I] K⟩₄₀
policy ≔ whnfF ⊢ ⟨flipA [K I] K⟩₍₎
